# Windsurf Rules — Shared Knowledge Repository

This file is a thin alias. The **binding rules** live in [AI_GUIDELINES.md](AI_GUIDELINES.md).
Cascade (Windsurf AI) must follow the entirety of the rules defined there.

## Project context

Knowledge-management repository for AI agents. Transforms knowledge extracted from real projects into reusable skills and agents, organized by **domain-first taxonomy** (`llm/`, `sfad/`, …).

## Cascade-specific notes

- Reply language: match the user. All generated repository content: English.
- Code, identifiers, file names, commit messages: English.
- Use relative links between files; never absolute or external links to local files.
- An agent requires ≥ 2 included skills; never create an agent with one skill.
- Before creating any new file, check for affinity with existing siblings in the same domain folder.

## Naming and locations

- Patterns: `knowledge/<domain>/patterns/SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE.md`
- Decisions: `knowledge/<domain>/decisions/kebab-case.md`
- Domain notes: `knowledge/<domain>/domain/kebab-case.md`
- Skills: `skills/<domain>/<class>/kebab-case.md`
- Agents: `agents/<domain>/kebab-case.md`

## Affinity priorities

| Affinity detected | Action |
| --- | --- |
| Same domain + same pattern | Update existing file |
| Same domain, different pattern | Create new skill + cross-link |
| Different domain, similar pattern | Create new skill with cross-reference |
| Same target agent | Add skill to existing agent |
| Genuinely new domain | Create the full `skills/<new>/`, `agents/<new>/`, `knowledge/<new>/{patterns,decisions,domain}/` tree |

